.TH BINLOG-STREAMER 1 "" "binlog-streamer" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
binlog-streamer \- MySQL binary log relay for independent replicas
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B binlog-streamer
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B binlog-streamer
receives the binary log from one MySQL or Percona Server source
(8.0 and newer), keeps it for a configured period and serves it to many
replicas, so the source carries one replication connection instead of one
per replica.
It normally runs as the systemd service
.BR binlog-streamer.service .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Settings file (default:
.IR /etc/binlog-streamer/settings.yml ).
.TP
.B \-\-validate\-config
Check the settings and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-rebuild\-index
With the relay stopped, write binlog.index anew from the binary logs in
data_dir and exit.
The files have to make one history: one basename, consecutive numbers,
and each file's Previous_gtids holding those of the one before;
otherwise the index is left as it is.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show the help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/binlog-streamer/settings.yml
Relay settings.
.TP
.I /etc/binlog-streamer/source.yml
Connection to the source.
.TP
.I /etc/binlog-streamer/replica.yml
Where replicas connect and their accounts.
.TP
.I /etc/default/binlog-streamer
Extra command-line options for the service.
.TP
.I /var/lib/binlog-streamer
Stored binary log files.
.SH SEE ALSO
.I /usr/share/doc/binlog-streamer/README.md
